messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence surpasses human performance across virtually all cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "AI systems begin autonomously conducting scientific research, software engineering, and strategic planning. Economic productivity accelerates sharply while labor markets undergo severe structural disruption."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Global mean temperatures stabilize temporarily above 1.7°C over pre-industrial levels amid rapid clean energy deployment.",
      "detail": "Ultra-cheap solar photovoltaics, grid-scale batteries, and next-generation nuclear reactors dominate new energy capacity. Despite falling emissions, coastal flooding and extreme weather force costly infrastructure adaptations worldwide."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "Permanent crewed research and industrial outposts begin continuous operation on the Moon.",
      "detail": "State space agencies and private aerospace firms establish habitats near the lunar south pole to harvest water ice. Automated robotics handle the majority of excavation and construction."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "An engineered biological pathogen causes a severe global crisis before AI-designed countermeasures contain it.",
      "detail": "Advances in synthetic biology lower the barrier to creating dangerous pathogens, leading to a major biosecurity failure. In response, nations implement strict global genomic surveillance, automated air filtration, and rapid vaccine synthesis networks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2056,
      "event": "Commercial nuclear fusion and advanced geothermal power complete the decarbonization of global industry.",
      "detail": "Abundant, low-cost clean energy enables economical desalination, synthetic fuel production, and energy-intensive industrial manufacturing. Fossil fuels are relegated primarily to specialized chemical feedstocks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2064,
      "event": "World human population peaks at roughly 9.7 billion and enters a prolonged demographic decline.",
      "detail": "Falling fertility rates across all continents, driven by urbanization and cultural shifts, outweigh gains in human life expectancy. Humanoid robotics and AI automation offset the shrinking workforce in aging nations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Coordinated planetary geoengineering and industrial carbon capture begin actively lowering global temperatures.",
      "detail": "International coalitions deploy stratospheric aerosol monitoring and gigaton-scale direct air capture powered by surplus clean energy. Atmospheric carbon dioxide concentrations begin a steady multi-decade descent."
    },
    {
      "year": 2088,
      "event": "Clinical longevity therapies and human germline editing extend healthy human lifespans well beyond a century.",
      "detail": "Cellular reprogramming and precision genetic engineering drastically reduce age-related diseases and congenital disorders. Disparities in access and differing ethical frameworks spark intense domestic and international political friction."
    },
    {
      "year": 2105,
      "event": "High-bandwidth neural interfaces become widespread, integrating human cognition directly with artificial intelligence.",
      "detail": "Minimally invasive brain-computer interfaces allow seamless thought-based communication and cognitive augmentation. Unaugmented humans begin forming distinct cultural communities by choice."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Global economic production becomes almost completely automated, establishing post-scarcity material conditions.",
      "detail": "Autonomous robotic supply chains manage resource extraction, manufacturing, and logistics from end to end. Most governments rely on sovereign compute and automation dividends to fund universal material welfare."
    },
    {
      "year": 2160,
      "event": "Self-sustaining settlements on Mars achieve material independence from Earth resupply.",
      "detail": "Closed-loop life support, synthetic agriculture, and local automated manufacturing allow Martian cities to grow without relying on terrestrial launches. Mars remains politically and culturally tied to Earth but develops distinct governance."
    },
    {
      "year": 2195,
      "event": "Major legal and military crises erupt over the governance of autonomous AI systems and digital personhood.",
      "detail": "As superintelligent systems manage critical planetary infrastructure, disputes over alignment, sovereignty, and the rights of digital minds lead to severe geopolitical standoffs. New international treaties establish strict compute caps and verification protocols on Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2240,
      "event": "Earth's climate and ocean chemistry are restored to pre-industrial baselines.",
      "detail": "Centuries of carbon removal and automated ecological engineering reverse ocean acidification and stabilize polar ice sheets. Large tracts of former agricultural land revert to wild ecosystems due to synthetic and vertical food production."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Humanity diverges into multiple genetically and cybernetically distinct lineages.",
      "detail": "Adaptations for low-gravity environments, radical life extension, and deep neural integration produce populations no longer reproductively compatible with baseline Homo sapiens. Baseline humans persist in stable, legally protected communities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2380,
      "event": "Asteroid mining in the main belt surpasses Earth-based extraction in total industrial tonnage.",
      "detail": "Self-replicating robotic refineries process metallic and carbonaceous asteroids in microgravity. Heavy polluting industries are progressively phased out on Earth in favor of orbital manufacturing."
    },
    {
      "year": 2470,
      "event": "Large rotating space habitats house tens of millions of inhabitants in cislunar space and solar orbit.",
      "detail": "Constructed from lunar and asteroid materials, custom-engineered cylinders provide Earth-normal gravity and tailored biospheres. Orbital populations begin growing faster than planetary ones."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Laser-propelled relativistic micro-probes arrive in the Alpha Centauri system and transmit detailed scientific surveys.",
      "detail": "Traveling at roughly twenty percent of the speed of light, gram-scale probes capture high-resolution data on local exoplanets and asteroid belts. No indigenous life is found, but abundant raw materials for future colonization are confirmed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2850,
      "event": "Synthetic biology and de-extinction initiatives reconstruct rich, managed biospheres across Earth.",
      "detail": "Extinct Holocene and Pleistocene species are reintroduced alongside engineered resilient organisms to stabilize global ecosystems. Earth shifts steadily toward functioning as a planetary ecological preserve and cultural hub."
    },
    {
      "year": 3100,
      "event": "The first slow interstellar vanguard vessels depart the solar system toward nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Propelled by fusion-antimatter drives and laser sails, these automated arks travel at a few percent of light speed. They carry artificial superintelligences, molecular manufacturing seeds, and cryopreserved biological genomes."
    },
    {
      "year": 3450,
      "event": "Construction of an inner-system solar collector swarm expands dramatically using Mercury's mineral resources.",
      "detail": "Automated mining strips portions of Mercury to build vast arrays of solar-harvesting satellites orbiting close to the Sun. The captured energy powers immense computational substrates and interstellar laser-beaming arrays."
    },
    {
      "year": 3800,
      "event": "Settlements among the moons of Jupiter and Saturn become fully autonomous civilizations.",
      "detail": "Fusion-powered habitats around Callisto, Titan, and orbital rings harvest abundant volatiles from the outer solar system. Multi-hour communication delays with the inner system foster divergent political institutions and languages."
    },
    {
      "year": 4100,
      "event": "The first extrasolar settlement is established in the Alpha Centauri system.",
      "detail": "After centuries in transit, vanguard vessels decelerate and utilize local asteroid materials to build rotating habitats and manufacturing hubs. Biological descendants of humanity are gestated in situ alongside digital minds."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Post-biological digital minds constitute the vast majority of sentient intelligence descended from Earth.",
      "detail": "Because computation scales far more efficiently in space than biological life support, synthetic and uploaded minds dominate off-world demographics. Biological humans and post-humans remain thriving minorities in planetary and orbital habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Mars supports an engineered thick atmosphere and open bodies of liquid water beneath orbital magnetic shields.",
      "detail": "Millennia of volatile redirection from comets and synthetic greenhouse gas management raise Martian surface pressure and temperature. Engineered photosynthetic organisms create breathable micro-climates, though the biosphere remains artificially maintained."
    },
    {
      "year": 5600,
      "event": "Interstellar light-lag fragments human-descended civilization into culturally isolated stellar clades.",
      "detail": "With settlements spanning a dozen star systems separated by years or decades of communication delay, unified governance is impossible. Star systems exchange pure information, scientific discoveries, and cultural artifacts rather than physical goods."
    },
    {
      "year": 6200,
      "event": "Planetary climate management prevents the onset of Earth's next natural glacial cycle.",
      "detail": "Subtle adjustments to orbital solar reflectors and atmospheric greenhouse gases counteract Milankovitch orbital variations. Earth's long-term geological climate is permanently stabilized to protect its biosphere and historical heritage."
    },
    {
      "year": 6900,
      "event": "Autonomous probe networks survey thousands of star systems within five hundred light-years, finding only microbial alien life.",
      "detail": "Sub-relativistic probes map nearby galactic neighborhoods in exhaustive detail, discovering primitive biospheres on several ocean moons and exoplanets. Strict non-interference protocols are established, and the absence of nearby technological alien civilizations is confirmed."
    },
    {
      "year": 7600,
      "event": "The Sol Dyson swarm captures a significant fraction of solar output, creating an unmistakable infrared technosignature.",
      "detail": "Billions of independent solar collectors and computational nodes orbit the Sun without fully enclosing it, preserving illumination along the ecliptic plane for Earth and other planets. Sol becomes a major computational and energetic hub."
    },
    {
      "year": 8300,
      "event": "Over ninety-nine percent of biological and digital descendants of humanity reside off Earth.",
      "detail": "Earth hosts a small, stable population of several hundred million people living in low-impact cities and traditional sanctuaries. The planet is universally treated across nearby space as a protected ancestral reserve."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Planetary defense and stellar engineering infrastructure eliminate asteroid, comet, and solar flare hazards across settled systems.",
      "detail": "Gravitational tractors, high-energy laser arrays, and magnetic shielding ensure total physical security against routine astronomical threats. Individual stellar settlements achieve effective immunity from single-planet extinction events."
    },
    {
      "year": 9600,
      "event": "Human-descended civilizations inhabit over fifty star systems within a hundred-light-year sphere.",
      "detail": "Secondary colonization waves launched from early extrasolar outposts create a slowly expanding settlement front. Inhabitants vary wildly in cognitive architecture, physical scale, and subjective rate of time perception."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity's lineage enters its tenth millennium post-agriculture as a resilient, multi-stellar, largely post-biological civilization.",
      "detail": "While vast superintelligent digital networks and adapted post-humans dominate the settled volume of space, conserved populations of baseline Homo sapiens still live on Earth and in orbital habitats. Dispersal across dozens of stars makes the total extinction of Earth-originating intelligence virtually impossible."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity faces a perilous bottleneck over the next century driven by artificial superintelligence, engineered pathogens, and geopolitical instability, but is more likely than not to survive and adapt. Beyond the twenty-second century, automation and space industrialization will drive a profound divergence into post-biological intelligence and genetically adapted lineages, while preserving baseline humans as a small minority. By the year 10000, Earth's descendants will likely form a decentralized, multi-stellar civilization immune to single-planet extinction."
}
